# Patch:  PrismML Bonsai 1-bit / ternary (Q1_0, PQ1_0, PQ2_0, TQ1_0) support
# Repo:   https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp
# Branch: merge/upstream-20261011
# Head:   31eb0812d370ec17c899edd9dfee223b390340fc
# Base:   b11645
# Exclude: tests/*
#
# PrismML's fork carrying the low-bit quant types, FWHT/Hadamard rotation and
# backend kernels needed to run prism-ml/Bonsai-27B-gguf (1-bit) and
# prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-27B-gguf (2-bit). The fork's default 'prism' branch
# lags upstream by ~1000 commits; 'merge/upstream-20261011' is the same work
# rebased onto recent master, so it is the one tracked here. tests/ is excluded:
# its CMakeLists conflicts with upstream and LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF anyway.
#
# After a refresh, drop the "+#include <vector>" hunk from src/llama-ext.h if
# upstream already has that include, otherwise patch skips the whole file as
# "reversed".
#
# b11642 is a hand rebase of the Head above (the fork had no newer merge
# branch): common/speculative.cpp and src/models/dflash.cpp re-anchored around
# upstream's LiLiCorr changes, ggml-sycl PQ2_0/PTQ1_0 cases placed after the
# new IQ3_* ones, and ggml-cuda/gated_delta_net.cu keeps upstream's new MMA
# path but skips it for raw gates and the fused state gather. On CUDA,
# qwen35 ubatches of >= 64 tokens therefore keep activated gates and the
# unfused state gather, so prefill takes the MMA path (+5-6% pp on a 4080S
# with Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B); decode and MTP verify keep the raw-gate fusion.
# A 'refresh'
# against an unchanged Head would undo that, so only refresh once the fork
# publishes a newer merge branch.
